From 298b81c7686ea3f8335577df8b3740bac9537d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mudzy992 <arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(e2e): a server-side command that ensures the harness
 actors exist

`provisionTestActors` creates USER and AGENT through the admin API, so it needs a
super-admin session first. On a stack whose install wizard was completed by hand
the only super admin is the founder account, which is not `E2E_SUPERADMIN_EMAIL`:
the harness has nobody to sign in as, `global-setup` fails within a minute and the
run reads like a product failure. e2e/README.md told the operator to create that
account in the UI; this makes it one command.

`node dist/src/cli/ensure-e2e-actors.js` reads the three actors from the
environment (`E2E_*_EMAIL` / `E2E_*_PASSWORD`, same defaults as the harness) or
from a JSON document on stdin (`--stdin`), creates a missing one as an ordinary
local account and aligns an existing one - password, home unit, role,
`mustChangePassword`, `isActive`. It goes through the primitives the API uses
(`ensureSystemRole`, `assignUserRole`, the SuperAdmin local-only invariant, the
authorization-cache invalidation) rather than writing rows itself, so what it
leaves behind is an account the product would recognise.

Passwords never travel in argv (`ps`, shell history, the exec session); the CI
step pipes them over the SSH access the job already has.

Refused, and reported per actor with exit 3: an address that is not disposable
(`e2e.*` or `E2E_ALLOW_REAL_ACCOUNTS`, the rule from
`e2e/helpers/disposable-account.ts` - this command overwrites passwords), a
directory-managed account (its password belongs to Entra/AD), an anonymized
account, and a password the offline policy rejects (`--allow-policy-violation`
overrides). An enrolled second factor is reported, not removed (`--reset-mfa`
removes it). A role this command had to create is flagged as empty until
`cli/seed-default-role-permissions.js` runs.

The CI step is opt-in (`E2E_ENSURE_ACTORS=true`, `E2E_BACKEND_CONTAINER` optional)
and off by default, so nothing changes for a stack that already has its actors.
